,{"class":172},[162,396,398,400,403,405,407,410,412,415,417,419,422,425],{"class":164,"line":397},9,[162,399,210],{"class":209},[162,401,402],{"class":176}," json ",[162,404,216],{"class":172},[162,406,371],{"class":176},[162,408,409],{"class":172},"&&",[162,411,338],{"class":172},[162,413,414],{"class":227}," TextDecoder",[162,416,303],{"class":176},[162,418,224],{"class":172},[162,420,421],{"class":227},"decode",[162,423,424],{"class":176},"(bytes)",[162,426,196],{"class":172},[162,428,430],{"class":164,"line":429},10,[162,431,203],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":202},[162,433,435,437,439,441,444,446],{"class":164,"line":434},11,[162,436,316],{"class":168},[162,438,264],{"class":176},[162,440,224],{"class":172},[162,442,443],{"class":227},"unload",[162,445,303],{"class":176},[162,447,196],{"class":172},[449,450,452],"h2",{"id":451},"the-session-path-is-not-a-file","The session path is not a file",[122,454,455,456,459,460,463],{},"The first argument of ",[126,457,458],{},"KeyringSession.load(path, password)"," is ",[131,461,462],{},"not"," a path on disk, on any OS. It\nis a logical id: the plugin hashes it, together with the client, vault and record names, into the\naccount name of each OS keyring entry.",[465,466,467,480],"table",{},[468,469,470],"thead",{},[471,472,473,477],"tr",{},[474,475,476],"th",{},"You pass",[474,478,479],{},"Effect",[481,482,483,492,500],"tbody",{},[471,484,485,489],{},[486,487,488],"td",{},"The same string on every platform",[486,490,491],{},"The same namespace everywhere (the usual case).",[471,493,494,497],{},[486,495,496],{},"Different strings",[486,498,499],{},"Separate namespaces, e.g. one per user or per wallet.",[471,501,502,508],{},[486,503,504,505],{},"Something that looks like a path, e.g. ",[126,506,507],{},"\u002Fwallet\u002Fmain",[486,509,510],{},"Fine: it is only a label, no folder has to exist.",[122,512,513],{},"Use stable ASCII-like ids. Changing the id later makes the old entries unreachable through the API\n(they stay in the OS store).",[449,515,517],{"id":516},"the-password-is-not-checked","The password is not checked",[122,519,520,523,524,527,528,531,532,535,536,224],{},[126,521,522],{},"password"," exists for Stronghold compatibility. It is ",[131,525,526],{},"not verified",": any password opens any\nsession, and it encrypts nothing. Rust wipes it at once and never stores or compares it. Pass ",[126,529,530],{},"\"\"","\nunless you are migrating code that already passes one. Access control comes from the OS store and\nthe plugin ",[148,533,534],{"href":55},"permissions","; see ",[148,537,50],{"href":51},[449,539,541],{"id":540},"session-lifetime","Session lifetime",[543,544,545,556,562,574,580],"ul",{},[546,547,548,551,552,555],"li",{},[126,549,550],{},"KeyringSession.load"," (",[126,553,554],{},"initialize",") adds the path to an in-memory list of loaded sessions of this process.",[546,557,558,559,224],{},"Store, vault and procedure calls on a path that is not loaded fail with\n",[126,560,561],{},"session not initialized: \u003Cpath>",[546,563,564,551,567,570,571,573],{},[126,565,566],{},"session.unload()",[126,568,569],{},"destroy",") removes the path from the list. The entries are ",[131,572,462],{}," deleted.",[546,575,576,579],{},[126,577,578],{},"session.save()"," writes nothing (every write is already in the OS store) but fails like Stronghold\nwhen the session is not loaded.",[546,581,582,583,585],{},"The list is per process: after an app restart call ",[126,584,228],{}," again.",[449,587,588],{"id":137},"Clients",[122,590,591,594,595,598,599,602,603,594,606,609],{},[126,592,593],{},"session.createClient(name)"," and ",[126,596,597],{},"session.loadClient(name)"," do the same thing: check that the session\nis loaded and return a ",[126,600,601],{},"KeyringClient",". A client needs no creation in the OS store; both exist for\nStronghold parity. ",[126,604,605],{},"client.getStore()",[126,607,608],{},"client.getVault(name)"," make no IPC call.",[449,611,612],{"id":141},"Store",[465,614,615,625],{},[468,616,617],{},[471,618,619,622],{},[474,620,621],{},"Method",[474,623,624],{},"Does",[481,626,627,644,658],{},[471,628,629,634],{},[486,630,631],{},[126,632,633],{},"get(key)",[486,635,636,637,640,641,224],{},"Resolves to the bytes (",[126,638,639],{},"Uint8Array",") or ",[126,642,643],{},"null",[471,645,646,651],{},[486,647,648],{},[126,649,650],{},"insert(key, value, lifetime?)",[486,652,653,654,657],{},"Writes the record, replacing an existing one. ",[126,655,656],{},"lifetime"," is ignored: OS stores have no expiry.",[471,659,660,665],{},[486,661,662],{},[126,663,664],{},"remove(key)",[486,666,667,668,224],{},"Deletes the record and resolves to its previous bytes, or ",[126,669,643],{},[122,671,672,673,676,677,679,680,683],{},"Values are ",[126,674,675],{},"number[]"," or ",[126,678,639],{},". Store the text of JSON with ",[126,681,682],{},"TextEncoder"," as above.",[449,685,687],{"id":686},"text-or-byte-ids","Text or byte ids",[122,689,690,691,693,694,697,698,700,701,704,705,708,709,224],{},"Client, vault, record and store key names may be strings or bytes (",[126,692,639],{},", ",[126,695,696],{},"ArrayBuffer",",\n",[126,699,675],{},"). A byte id that equals the UTF-8 of a text id is the ",[131,702,703],{},"same"," id: ",[126,706,707],{},"store.get([107])","\nreads the record written with ",[126,710,711],{},"store.insert(\"k\", …)",[449,713,715],{"id":714},"how-names-become-entries","How names become entries",[122,717,718],{},"Every record is one OS keyring entry under your service name. Its account is built from the first\n8 bytes (16 hex characters) of the SHA-256 of each name:",[465,720,721,731],{},[468,722,723],{},[471,724,725,728],{},[474,726,727],{},"Kind",[474,729,730],{},"Account",[481,732,733,743],{},[471,734,735,738],{},[486,736,737],{},"Store record",[486,739,740],{},[126,741,742],{},"kp:v1:\u003Csession>:\u003Cclient>:st:\u003Ckey>",[471,744,745,748],{},[486,746,747],{},"Vault record",[486,749,750],{},[126,751,752],{},"kp:v1:\u003Csession>:\u003Cclient>:v:\u003Cvault>:\u003Crecord>",[122,754,755,756,759,760,764,765,224],{},"So names of any length fit OS limits, and the OS store shows only hashes. The ",[126,757,758],{},"kp:"," prefix is\nreserved: the ",[148,761,763],{"href":762},"\u002Fguides\u002Fpasswords#reserved-accounts","password commands"," refuse it so the webview cannot\nread vault keys through ",[126,766,767],{},"getPasswords",[122,769,770,771,774,775,224],{},"Values are stored as Base64 text. On Windows this limits a store record or vault secret to about\n",[131,772,773],{},"960 bytes",", see ",[148,776,97],{"href":98},[122,778,779],{},"The OS stores cannot list entries, so neither can the plugin: keep your own index of keys if you\nneed one.",[781,782,783],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .s7zQu, html code.shiki .s7zQu{--shiki-light:#39ADB5;--shiki-light-font-style:italic;--shiki-default:#89DDFF;--shiki-default-font-style:italic;--shiki-dark:#89DDFF;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic}html pre.shiki code .sMK4o, html code.shiki .sMK4o{--shiki-light:#39ADB5;--shiki-default:#89DDFF;--shiki-dark:#89DDFF}html pre.shiki code .sTEyZ, html code.shiki .sTEyZ{--shiki-light:#90A4AE;--shiki-default:#EEFFFF;--shiki-dark:#BABED8}html pre.shiki code .sfazB, html code.shiki .sfazB{--shiki-light:#91B859;--shiki-default:#C3E88D;--shiki-dark:#C3E88D}html pre.shiki code .spNyl, html code.shiki .spNyl{--shiki-light:#9C3EDA;--shiki-default:#C792EA;--shiki-dark:#C792EA}html pre.shiki code .s2Zo4, html code.shiki .s2Zo4{--shiki-light:#6182B8;--shiki-default:#82AAFF;--shiki-dark:#82AAFF}html .light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-light-text-decoration);}html.light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-l